# Generated files (large SQL dumps)
# Keep the examples/ sample but ignore other large outputs
*.sql
!examples/*.sql
# clear_demo.sql is SOURCE, not a generated dump -- the blanket *.sql rule was silently excluding it, so a
# fix to it could be committed with `git add -A` and simply vanish. It is the script that decides which
# tables a load wipes, which makes it the most consequential file here.
!clear_demo.sql

